                <pb facs="0799" n="685" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg685"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.51/741</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Alternate Chairman of the International Committee
                        of Bankers on Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">T.
                            Cochran</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-16"><hi rendition="#italic">May 16,
                        1922</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received May 17.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: In Mr. Lamont’s absence I beg to
                    advise you that Mr. de la Huerta, the Mexican Minister of Finance, has notified
                    us that he, together with his associates, will come to New York for conferences
                    with this Committee, beginning June 2nd. We have further been advised that Mr.
                    de la Huerta will leave Mexico for the United States on May 21st.</p>
                <p>Mr. Lamont expects to sail from England on May 24th. He will be accompanied by
                    representatives of the British and French Sections of the International
                    Committee, who are coining for the purpose of attending the conferences with Mr.
                    de la Huerta.</p>
                <p>With great respect [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomas Cochran</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
